CAT = "polJudgment"; SEG = "JDG"
Q = [
("On a burglary call you see a fellow officer take cash from the scene and put it in his pocket. What should you do?",
 "Report it to a supervisor", ["Talk to him later in private", "Ignore it unless it happens again", "Write it in your notes only"],
 "Theft by an officer is serious misconduct and must be reported up the chain. Handling it privately or staying quiet makes you part of it."),
("A store owner offers you a free meal for keeping an eye on the place. What should you do?",
 "Politely decline the offer", ["Accept it once to be friendly", "Accept and patrol there more", "Accept but pay half the price"],
 "Gifts tied to extra police service create a duty to the giver. Decline politely; the store gets the same service as everyone else."),
("Driving to a minor theft report, you see a person collapse on the sidewalk. What should you do?",
 "Help the person and call medics", ["Continue to the theft call", "Ask a passerby to call 911", "Notify dispatch and keep driving"],
 "A possible medical emergency outranks a minor property report. Stop, tell dispatch, get medics coming and give aid."),
("A man yells insults at you while you write a parking ticket. What is the best response?",
 "Stay calm and finish the job", ["Arrest him for the insults", "Yell back to show authority", "Tear up the ticket and leave"],
 "Insults alone are not a crime, and reacting escalates the situation. Stay professional and finish the task."),
("Your sergeant gives an order you think is unwise but that is not illegal or unsafe. What should you do?",
 "Follow it, then discuss it later", ["Refuse until it is fully explained", "Ask other officers to vote", "Report the sergeant at once"],
 "Lawful, safe orders are followed. Raise your concerns afterward through the chain of command."),
("A supervisor orders you to do something clearly illegal. What should you do?",
 "Decline and report it up the chain", ["Obey, since orders come first", "Obey it and complain afterward in writing", "Ask your partner to do it instead"],
 "No order makes an illegal act lawful. Decline and report it to a higher supervisor."),
("You stop a car for speeding and find the driver is your neighbor. What should you do?",
 "Handle it as for any driver", ["Let him go since you know him", "Give a ticket to avoid favoritism", "Ask him for a favor in return"],
 "Treat him exactly as you would a stranger. Letting him go or being harsher because you know him are both unfair."),
("You find a mistake in a report you already turned in. What should you do?",
 "Tell a supervisor and correct it", ["Leave it unless someone notices", "Rewrite and replace it quietly", "Wait to fix it until it goes to court"],
 "Errors are corrected openly, usually with a supplemental report. Swapping the report quietly looks like falsifying it."),
("A lost child walks up to you at a busy festival. What should you do first?",
 "Stay with the child and call it in", ["Send the child to the info booth", "Tell the child to look for parents", "Leave the child to search the crowd"],
 "Keep the child with you so the child is safe, and radio a description so the parents can be found. Never send a lost child off alone."),
("A friend asks you to run a license plate on the police computer for a personal reason. What should you do?",
 "Refuse; it is for official use only", ["Run it if it is just this once", "Run it but do not share the address", "Ask a coworker to run it for you"],
 "Police databases are for official business only. Running a plate for a friend is misuse even if you keep the result to yourself."),
("You see another officer use clearly excessive force on a handcuffed suspect. What should you do?",
 "Step in and report it", ["Wait and discuss it later", "Leave the scene quietly", "Help hold the suspect down"],
 "Officers are expected to intervene to stop clearly excessive force and to report it. Staying silent is a failure of duty."),
("Two calls come in at once: a burglary in progress and a report of a bike stolen yesterday. Which do you handle first?",
 "The burglary in progress", ["The stolen bike, since it is quicker", "Whichever is closer", "The one received first"],
 "A crime in progress puts people at risk and offers a chance to catch the suspect. The old theft report can wait."),
("An elderly man keeps calling about noise that you cannot hear when you arrive. What is the best approach?",
 "Check it and talk to him kindly", ["Tell him to stop calling", "Warn him about making false reports", "Ignore future calls from him"],
 "Check the complaint and treat him with respect. Repeated calls can point to a real problem or a need for other services."),
("Off duty in a store, you see a shoplifter. Your agency tells off-duty officers to act as good witnesses unless a life is in danger. What should you do?",
 "Watch closely and call it in", ["Chase and tackle the shoplifter", "Confront him and show your badge", "Do nothing since you are off duty"],
 "Follow the policy: observe, get a good description and call on-duty officers. Acting alone off duty is risky for everyone."),
("A man you arrested spits at you, then stops resisting while handcuffed. What should you do?",
 "Use no more force; document it", ["Strike him once to stop it", "Tighten the cuffs as a lesson", "Release him to cool things down"],
 "Once a person is controlled, more force is punishment, not control. Document the spitting, which can be charged."),
("A reporter at a scene asks you for the victim's name. What should you do?",
 "Refer him to the information officer", ["Give the name if it's been confirmed", "Give the name off the record", "Tell him to search social media"],
 "Most agencies release information through a designated public information officer, after families are told."),
("Your partner is often late, and you have been covering for him. What is the best step?",
 "Talk to him, then a supervisor", ["Keep covering for him to protect him", "Complain about him to others", "Ask for a new partner quietly"],
 "Raise it with him directly first, and go to a supervisor if it continues. Covering for him is dishonest."),
("A driver you stopped offers you money to forget the ticket. What should you do?",
 "Refuse and treat it as a bribe", ["Laugh it off and write the ticket", "Accept it and turn it in later", "Give a warning instead"],
 "Offering money to an officer is bribery. Refuse it and document and report the offer."),
("A resident asks you for directions while you are on your way to a non-emergency call. What should you do?",
 "Briefly help, then continue", ["Ignore the resident and drive on", "Escort the resident there yourself", "Tell them to look it up online"],
 "A quick answer serves the public without delaying the call much. A long escort leaves the call waiting."),
("At a crash scene, a bystander is filming you but is not interfering. What should you do?",
 "Let them film and keep working", ["Take the phone as evidence", "Order them to stop recording", "Make them delete the video at once"],
 "In the United States people may generally record police in public places. Act only if the person interferes with the work."),
("At a domestic call, the caller now says through the closed door that everything is fine. What should you do?",
 "Confirm everyone inside is safe", ["Leave, because the caller canceled it", "Force the door immediately", "Ask dispatch to close the call"],
 "Victims are sometimes pressured to cancel. Make contact and confirm everyone is safe before you leave."),
("A new policy changes how evidence must be logged, and you prefer the old way. What should you do?",
 "Follow the new policy", ["Keep using the old method", "Use whichever is faster", "Wait until training on it"],
 "Policies apply once they take effect. You can suggest changes, but you follow the current rule."),
("While serving a search warrant at a house, you find a large amount of cash. What should you do?",
 "Count and log it with a witness", ["Count it later back at the station", "Leave it where it was found", "Log an estimate of the total"],
 "Count and record cash right away, ideally with a witness or supervisor, so no one can question what was found."),
("A distraught mother is shouting and demanding that you find her missing son right now. What is the best response?",
 "Stay calm and gather the details", ["Tell her to calm down or leave", "Promise her he will be found today", "Wait until she stops shouting"],
 "Her fear is understandable. Calmly get a description and where he was last seen, and do not make promises you cannot keep."),
("You learn that a close friend on the force has been falsifying overtime records. What should you do?",
 "Report it through proper channels", ["Warn him privately and give him time", "Say nothing to protect him", "Wait to see if it happens again"],
 "Falsifying records is dishonesty that must be reported, whoever does it. Friendship does not change the duty."),
("You are guarding a crime scene, and a city council member asks to come in and look around. What should you do?",
 "Politely keep them out", ["Let them in briefly", "Let them in with an escort", "Ask them to sign in first"],
 "Only people with a job to do at the scene may enter. Rank or office outside the investigation does not give access."),
("While writing your report, you cannot remember whether you asked a certain question during an interview. What should you write?",
 "Only what you are sure of", ["That you did ask it", "That the suspect refused it", "What your partner suggests"],
 "A report must be truthful. Write what you know, and never fill a gap with something you are not sure happened."),
("A driver you stopped is upset and accuses you of stopping him because of his race. What should you do?",
 "Stay calm and explain the stop", ["End the stop and drive away at once", "Argue that you are not racist", "Add charges for the comment"],
 "Stay professional and explain the reason for the stop. Arguing or punishing the comment escalates things and is improper."),
("A crowd gathers and yells while you make an arrest. What is your priority?",
 "Secure the suspect and get backup", ["Answer each person's questions", "Release the suspect to calm the crowd", "Order everyone to go home"],
 "Control the suspect and call for help so the scene stays safe. Explaining to the crowd can come later."),
("You are first at a scene where a man is bleeding heavily from a leg wound. What do you do first?",
 "Apply pressure and call medics", ["Look for the person who did it", "Take photos before aid", "Interview the victim first"],
 "Saving life comes first. Heavy bleeding can kill in minutes, so control it and get medics coming."),
("In front of the public, another officer tells a joke that mocks an ethnic group. What should you do?",
 "Tell him it is not acceptable", ["Laugh along to keep the peace", "Ignore it since it was a joke", "Repeat it to other officers"],
 "Demeaning remarks damage public trust. Address it, and report it if it continues or the policy requires."),
("You realize you gave a crash victim the wrong case number. What should you do?",
 "Contact them and correct it", ["Wait for them to call about it", "Hope they look it up", "Note it in your file only"],
 "Fix your own mistake quickly so the person is not harmed by it."),
]
